From e57b06f2018570dae037bf579dcb058b481d3c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:48:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] ppc: add AltiVec blur

A stripe line is exactly one vector at alignment 16, so copy_line and
the zero line of c/blur_template.h become a load and a zero vector.

shrink_func sums four 15-bit values in int32, which does not fit in
16-bit lanes; it uses the same halving add chain as the NEON backend,
with the floor halving add synthesised from vec_avg.  expand_func and
stripe_pack/unpack are literal transcriptions because the C code already
computes in wrapping uint16_t.  The parametric filters accumulate into
two 32-bit vectors fed by vec_mule/vec_mulo.
---
 libass/ppc/blur_altivec.c | 456 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 456 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/blur_altivec.c

diff --git a/libass/ppc/blur_altivec.c b/libass/ppc/blur_altivec.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1cb663
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libass/ppc/blur_altivec.c
@@ -0,0 +1,456 @@
